WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.469
-You know what, guys?

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:05.070
Those were mostly
pretty good jokes, I think.

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.807
But our monologue writers
write pages and pages of jokes

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.376
every day and, um,

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.312
they're not all good
and, honestly, sometimes,

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.882
sometimes I think they just like
throw in some real stinkers,

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.718
just to fill up a page
and meet the assignment.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:21.220
Baze, I think that's
probably accurate, right?

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.923
So, anyways, Baze and I got
to talking, you know,

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.958
because it's understandable
that they fill out the pages,

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:28.060
but, we're about to have
audiences back

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.897
and, that kind of laziness
really has to stop,

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:34.467
which means it's time
for a "Surprise Inspection."

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.470
[ Trumpet plays march ]
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:42.708
♪♪

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:45.345
And then, maybe tomorrow
we'll do one for graphics?

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:49.482
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.883
So, here's how this works.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.685
These are real jokes

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.288
that were actually submitted
by our writers,

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:57.456
that are unusable for this show.

00:00:57.456 --> 00:00:58.891
Some are dumb,

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:02.796
some are patently offensive,
and some are baffling.

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:05.265
Most importantly, the writers
don't know we're doing this

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:08.034
and, because a lot of them
don't watch the show,

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.168
they'll never know
we're doing it.

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:11.771
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.672
Here we go.

00:01:13.672 --> 00:01:15.775
U.S. wildlife officials
announced today

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:18.878
that 22 animals and one plant
have become extinct,

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.814
including the Bachman's warbler.

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:25.652
Thankfully, Bachman's warbles
will live on forever,

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:28.654
♪ Taking care of business ♪

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:30.823
[ Laughter ]
So that --

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.959
that joke was dependent
on people knowing that song,

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:36.196
"Taking Care of Business,"
was performed

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:40.300
by Bachman-Turner Overdrive.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:45.271
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:50.043
The rare audible "Ugh"
from Shoemaker.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.678
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.813
That was Goldich?
That was Matt Goldich?

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:56.049
Let's take a look
at a photo of Goldich.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:57.316
There you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.316 --> 00:01:58.585
That's the man
who wrote that joke.

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:00.019
That's the face he made
when we told him

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.487
we were going to do it
in the show tonight.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.856
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:07.593
A house outside --
Alright, here we go.

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:10.062
A house outside of Boston
that recently caught fire

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:13.332
and partially burned down
was listed for sale last month.

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:16.936
For more on this, check out...

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:21.173
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:24.143
So that's a joke where,
either you've seen the film

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:27.046
and you're aghast
at the punch line;

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.280
or you haven't seen the film

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.883
and then, you would go,
you'd watch the film,

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:33.586
and then you would be aghast
after that.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:34.920
So that was courtesy of Ian.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.723
Let's take a look at Ian.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:39.893
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:44.397
Who, I guess, wrote that joke
and then, we took a photo of him

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.531
having an orgasm.

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:50.702
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.702 --> 00:02:53.373
The pharmaceutical company
Pfizer announced yesterday

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.475
that it has submitted data
to the FDA

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:59.411
about its coronavirus vaccine
in children ages five and older.

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:01.547
"Damn it, right when I got
to go to prison,"

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:03.015
said R. Kelly.

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:05.184
[ Laughter and oohs ]

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:09.822
Again, offensive, but way more
baffling than offensive.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:12.892
I mean,
I hate to defend the man.

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.061
But I feel like five

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:18.230
was a little younger
than the target

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.265
and this joke implies
that his fear --

00:03:20.265 --> 00:03:23.235
Go back up a card, Wally.

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:26.439
So, "Damn it, right when I go
to prison," because he was --

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:29.709
It implies that like his fear
was getting coronavirus.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.310
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.979
It just stinks.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.313
It was written by Mike Scollins.

00:03:34.313 --> 00:03:35.648
Let's take a look at him.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:38.718
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:45.157
Passengers
on a Spirit Airlines plane

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:46.425
in Atlantic City, New Jersey,

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:48.561
were forced to deplane
over the weekend

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.263
after a large bird caused
an engine fire,

00:03:51.263 --> 00:03:53.532
which is an extremely rude
thing to call

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:55.801
the flight attendant.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.403
A large bird.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:04:00.572
[ Laughter ]
So,

00:04:00.572 --> 00:04:03.443
I guess that would be like
British slang.

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:06.145
Like this would maybe work,

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:10.983
if it was British Airways
or Michael Caine Airlines.

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:12.619
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.754
Karen wrote that.
Let's take a look at her.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:15.822
There she is.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.122
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.122 --> 00:04:19.291
Shame on you, Karen.
Producers announced yesterday

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:22.127
that James Bond actor
Daniel Craig will next year star

00:04:22.127 --> 00:04:23.629
in a Broadway production
of "Macbeth."

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:24.797
Said Craig,

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:27.233
"The name's Beth.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.367
Macbeth."

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:31.404
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.909
Bryan wrote that.
Here he is.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:40.380
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.783
According to a new study --

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:47.620
Well, I hate to do this
to you, Wally.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.155
-What?
-I'm going to surprise inspect

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.822
your cue card.

00:04:50.822 --> 00:04:52.124
You wrote "new" twice.

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:54.060
-Oh, yeah.
-Turn it to the camera.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.029
-Which one?

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:57.429
-"According to a new new study."

00:04:57.429 --> 00:04:59.032
We caught Wally, too.

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:01.100
-It could've been really new.
-What?

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.668
-It could've been like
really new,

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:03.903
so that's why we wrote --
[ Laughs ]

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:05.171
-Do you think that's
how scientists say it?

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:06.872
"We have a new, new study."

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:08.741
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah, probably not.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.110
-You guys.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.012
-Probably not.
Okay.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:15.948
-According to a new,
new study...

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:18.651
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:21.253
...mice have feelings
of sadness and depression.

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:23.890
Asked scientists,
"Did they say if it was because

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.324
of the cancer we gave them?"

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:28.494
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:32.998
So, again -- Ally wrote that.

00:05:32.998 --> 00:05:35.801
Let's take a look at Ally.

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:37.870
So there was a new study,

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:41.174
so a different set of scientists
did the study

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:43.442
and then the first set
of scientists

00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:48.648
read the study and was like,
"Uh-oh."

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:51.984
Today --
Oh, Scollins is back, everybody.

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:54.253
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:56.055
Today was National Vodka Day

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:58.724
and it's about to Popov.
[pop off]

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:02.895
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:04.297
See?
I could never --

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:05.798
I mean, there's like
courtesy laughs

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:09.301
from the people who work here
because they know Scollins.

00:06:09.301 --> 00:06:10.936
But like, once we have
strangers back,

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:13.539
they're going to be angry.

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.374
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:18.444
The Munich Airport in Germany
was put into lockdown last week

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.913
after a man allegedly tried
to go through security

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:22.447
with a live mortar shell

00:06:22.447 --> 00:06:24.616
that he forgot was
in his book bag.

00:06:24.616 --> 00:06:26.652
Said the man, "Oh, my God,

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:29.689
I should've eaten
this before getting here."

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:30.957
[ Quiet laughter ]

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:32.658
Nothing.
And they like you, Karen.

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.426
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.426 --> 00:06:35.962
The people here like you.

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:38.263
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.263 --> 00:06:40.532
In honor of Disney World's
50th anniversary,

00:06:40.532 --> 00:06:42.234
Southwest Airlines has unveiled

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:44.303
a commemorative
custom-designed plane

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:46.873
that features an outline
of Cinderella's Castle

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:49.007
on the outside, but head's up --

00:06:49.007 --> 00:06:51.377
the inside is still
full pumpkin.

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:52.912
-[ Chuckle ]

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:57.883
-The castle.

00:06:57.883 --> 00:07:01.420
Now, part of it --
Again, if it was

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:05.491
the carriage,
full pumpkin would maybe work.

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:08.227
The castle wasn't a pumpkin.

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:10.362
It's Ian again.
Let's take a look.

00:07:10.362 --> 00:07:11.464
Oh, he's fine.

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:16.802
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:18.504
Audiences are coming back.

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:22.608
[ Laughter ]
This is very serious.

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:25.545
And I feel like the seriousness
of this moment

00:07:25.545 --> 00:07:29.081
is going to be undercut
in a second

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:32.518
when we see
the title card again,

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:37.423
but I really want you guys
to start focusing on the work.

00:07:37.423 --> 00:07:39.258
This has been
"Surprise Inspection."

00:07:39.258 --> 00:07:42.261
[ Trumpet plays march ]
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:45.398
♪♪

